      "textEn": "404\n\nWhen uprooted, the tree falls immediately and begins to dry up. Similarly, if someone\ndoes not care about this body, which is considered untrue—that is, if this untrue\nis eradicated—then this body certainly dries up. Meaning: In this context, Srila Rupa Goswami says—\n\nBy the power of intellect, the object of detachment. Renunciation of the fruits of detachment is called the fruit of detachment. “The detachment of a person who, without knowing the relationship of objects to Krishna, excludes them,\nis incomplete.” (Bhaktirasamrit-Sindhu 1.2.266). If the body is engaged in the service of Krishna, then the body should not be considered material. Sometimes, the guru\nmay have confusion about the spiritual body. But Sheel Roop Goswami gives the sermon—\nBy the intellect, the object of detachment. One should not neglect the body completely devoted to the service of Krishna, considering it material. He who neglects, his detachment is false.\nIf the body is not properly\nnourished, then it falls and dries up like a tree uprooted from its roots, due to which further\nfruits and flowers cannot be taken. Therefore, it is the order of the Vedas—\nOm, thus is the truth, the untruth, that flower, fruit, and word, that which is truth, the Lord, the glorious, the auspicious, the fame. He who speaks the truth, speaks the truth, but if he speaks falsely, he is like a tree without roots; he withers.\nSimilarly, he who speaks falsely, speaks falsely, but does not do good to himself, he withers; he is like a tree without roots; he withers. Therefore, do not speak falsely, do not do good to yourself with this. The meaning is that the actions that are performed with the help of the body for the satisfaction of the ultimate truth (Om Tatsat),\nare never destroyed, even if they are accomplished by a perishable body. Undoubtedly, such\nworks are eternal. Therefore, the body should be taken care of properly. Because this body is not eternal, it is perishable. No one can let it be eaten by a lion, nor can it be allowed to be killed by any enemy.\nIt can be destroyed. All precautions should be taken to protect the body.\nParagrikamparanam va aksharam yattadotimiti."
